<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Hologram&nbsp;Recording</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Hologram&nbsp;Recording</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>The following message was translated by SCP-5144-1.<br />
The message is in an unknown language.<br />
The metal disk that dispenses the hologram message has great wear and barely functions.</strong></p>
<p><strong>&lt;Beginning Message Translation&gt;</strong></p>
<p>Unknown Figure:</p>
<p>It's been a long time Brother.<br />
I am sad you had to destroy yourself for those pitiful lifeforms below you. But you always were so fascinated by them. <em>*a chuckle*</em> You were always the one to look on the bright side of this painful existence. I remember when you turned the star ways I tore apart into beautiful tapestries of chaos. I do miss seeing them.</p>
<p>*a pause*</p>
<p>That world&#8230; You put so much time and love into that world. But why did you have to go destroy yourself for it? Was it worth it? All that pain?</p>
<p>*another pause*</p>
<p>My children have failed me. You are my last hope.<br />
I am imprisoned below the sand, and the child of light stands in the way of my freedom. If you are going to free me, you must destroy the child of light.<br />
Free me, Brother.<br />
So that I may destroy this painful existence, and you can create it a new from the ashes.<br />
Free me, Brother.</p>
<p><strong>&lt;End Message Translation&gt;</strong></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<hr />
<p><strong>Cross-Tests:</strong><br />
<strong>These are the logs of 3 cross-tests that all shared the similar feeling of Deja Vu from SCP-5144-1. No connection with the SCPs used for testing are found as of yet.</strong></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Cross&nbsp;Test&nbsp;SCP-5144-1&nbsp;and&nbsp;SCP-3000</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Cross&nbsp;Test&nbsp;SCP-5144-1&nbsp;and&nbsp;SCP-3000</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<div class="blockquote">
<p><strong>Cross Test:</strong> SCP-5144-1</p>
<p><strong>Cross Test:</strong> SCP-3000</p>
<p><strong>Foreword:</strong> To test 5144-1's immunity to cognitohazards, it was supposed to be introduced to the Y909 compound. However, 5144-1 insisted it go meet SCP-3000 face to face. The request was met with hesitation from head researchers but was accepted.</p>
<p><strong>&lt;Begin Test&gt;</strong></p>
<p>*SCP-5144-1 exits the SCPF Eremita. It was given a waterproof radio it carried in one robotic hand, as well as a glass flask in its right hand. 5144-1 was instructed to expose itself to the Y909 compound and attempt to collect some of the compound in the flask.*</p>
<p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;You are nearing SCP-3000. About 400 meters. Do you see anything?&quot;</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Nope. Damn its pitch black out here. What am I looking for again?&quot;</p>
<p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;SCP-3000 resembles a massive serpent or eel-like lifeform.&quot;</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;A big snake. Got it.&quot;</p>
<p>*5144-1 is now 200 meters from 3000*</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;I gotta say, it's nice being able to float around like I'm in space. No stars, just blackness&#8230; *sigh* peaceful.&quot;</p>
<p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;Please remain on task.&quot;</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Yea yea I know.&quot;</p>
<p>*5144-1 is now 120 meters from 3000*</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Uhh I think I found it.&quot;</p>
<p>*5144-1's tail flower casts a purple light across the face of SCP-3000. 3000 has started excreting the Y909 compound.*</p>
<p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;Please swim toward the Y909 substance.&quot;</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;You mean the dark liquid right&#8230; Ugh! Why did I sign up for this.&quot;</p>
<p>*5144-1 swam into the dark mass*</p>
<p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;Do you feel anything?&quot;</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Not rea- *5144-1 started gagging* Disgusting! The compound tastes like spoiled milk.&quot;</p>
<p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;Do you remember your task?&quot;</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Yep. Expose myself to some of the substance and then get a sample. I don't think I am forgetting anything.&quot;</p>
<p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;Movement to your left! What do you see?&quot;</p>
<p>*SCP-3000 had moved and was now looking at 5144-1*</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;A large mouth and a ton of teeth. Uh&#8230; Hello ma'am?&quot;</p>
<p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;Who are you speaking to?&quot;</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Who do ya think&#8230; The snake. Woah that's weird.&quot;</p>
<p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;What is?&quot;</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;This feels familiar, not the place but like, her. Like some weird Deja Vu. Maybe it's the Y909 stuff.&quot;</p>
<p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;Be careful. We don't know what will happen if you are consumed.&quot;</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Yea I know. She's kinda cute. Hah, she's smiling at me.&quot;</p>
<p>*3000 had opened its mouth*</p>
<p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;Mozart get out of the way!&quot;</p>
<p>*5144-1 barely swam out of the way. 2 robotic limbs had been ripped off and consumed by 3000.&quot;</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Woah there!&quot;</p>
<p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;Retrieve the Y909 substance and return.&quot;</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;On it.&quot;</p>
<p>*5144-1 swam near the back of 3000's head and filled the flask it carried with the compound.*</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Aight, got the compound. Heading back to the sub.&quot;</p>
<p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;5144-1 incoming!&quot;</p>
<p>*3000 lunged at 5144-1 again, this time biting off his tail*</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;<em>Jesus woman</em>! I'm like the first guy you've ever met who hasn't been scared to death by your face and you're already trying to kill me. No wonder you don't have a man!&quot;</p>
<p>*snickers are heard from Command's side of the radio*</p>
<p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;Get back here quick.&quot;</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Right.&quot;</p>
<p>*5144-1 returned to the Eremita's exit hatch and entered. It gave the vial to command and the Eremita resurfaced.*</p>
<p><strong>&lt;End Test&gt;</strong></p>
<p><strong>Closing Statement:</strong> SCP-3000's Y909 substance does not affect SCP-5144-1.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Cross&nbsp;Test&nbsp;SCP-5144-1&nbsp;and&nbsp;SCP-682</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Cross&nbsp;Test&nbsp;SCP-5144-1&nbsp;and&nbsp;SCP-682</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<div class="blockquote">
<p><strong>Cross Test:</strong> SCP-5144-1</p>
<p><strong>Cross Test:</strong> SCP-682</p>
<p><strong>Foreword:</strong> To test both SCP-5144-1 and SCP-682's immortality, they were put in a cell with instructions to terminate each other.</p>
<p><strong>&lt;Begin Test&gt;</strong></p>
<p>*SCP-5144-1 enters the cell. SCP-682 is visible on the side of the room opposite to 5144-1.*</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Hello SCP uh&#8230; 682. I am 5144-1, you can call me Mozart if you want.&quot; *5144-1 holds out hand as if to shake 682's hand*</p>
<p><strong>682:</strong> *Coming closer to 5144-1* &quot;You are an interesting creature, so I will not kill you yet.&quot;</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Thanks? I guess&#8230;&quot;</p>
<p><strong>682:</strong> &quot;What are you?&quot;</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Huh. What?&quot;</p>
<p><strong>682:</strong> &quot;I said, What are you?&quot;</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Oh. Hah, I don't even know. Am I a plant or animal? The day I find out, heh&#8230; that'll be the day.&quot;</p>
<p><strong>682:</strong> &quot;You feel&#8230; familiar somehow. I never have met you but you still seem familiar.&quot;</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Hmmm. You are right, I got the same feeling I got with the slime creature. Interesting&#8230;&quot;</p>
<p>*SCP-682's eyes widen*</p>
<p><strong>682:</strong> &quot;How did you come into creation?&quot;</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;I beg your pardon?&quot;</p>
<p><strong>682:</strong> *seeming slightly stressed* &quot;<em>How</em> did you come into creation?&quot;</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;I don't know. Kinda just woke up in the middle of the void. Why do you as-&quot;</p>
<p>*5144-1 is cut off by the sound of the intercom*</p>
<p><strong>Researcher:</strong> &quot;Ok SCP-5144-1, please let SCP-682 attempt to terminate you.&quot;</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Got it doc. *turning to 682* C'mon hit me with your best shot!&quot;</p>
<p>*SCP-682 attacked 5144-1. 5144-1 did not defend itself in any way. After 3 and a half minutes of 682 tearing apart 5144-1's body, 682 stopped.*</p>
<p><strong>Researcher:</strong> &quot;5144-1 you still alive?&quot;</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> *Now a severed head in the corner* &quot;Yea doc I'm good.&quot;</p>
<p>*5144-1 took 2 minutes and 53 seconds to reform.*</p>
<p><strong>Researcher:</strong> &quot;Ok now, SCP-5144-1, please terminate SCP-682.&quot;</p>
<p><strong>682:</strong> &quot;Ugh. Don't bother, he knows you can't kill me.&quot;</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;If that's true, then I'm sorry this is gonna hurt like hell.&quot;</p>
<p>*5144-1 raised its robotic arms and began firing its energy beams. Loud screams can be heard from 682. This went on for a continual 4 minutes of bombardment before 5144-1 ceased attack. 682 was only a charred corpse now.*</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> *sniffing the air* &quot;Oh no, looks like I overcooked dinner.&quot;</p>
<p><strong>682:</strong> &quot;I.. I'll kill you for that!&quot;</p>
<p>*682 lunged at 5144-1's leg and attempted to rip it off. However, 5144-1 leaped out of the way and then constrained 682 with its robotic arms.*</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Dude. You couldn't kill me in your full state, you ain't getting anything done looking like that. I guess I can try to help.&quot;</p>
<p>*5144-1 raised its right hand to face 682. Then it started to glow blue-ish and 682's body reformed at a rate drastically quicker than normal. Finishing in only 30 seconds.*</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Is that better?&quot;</p>
<p><strong>682:</strong> &quot;What the? How did you do that?&quot;</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;One of my *holding up fingers to form quotation symbols* anomalous abilities. Not as cool as being able to bend reality but still is fun.&quot;</p>
<p><strong>&lt;End Log&gt;</strong></p>
<p><strong>Closing Statement:</strong> SCP-5144-1 seems to have the same anomalous regeneration SCP-682 does. However, 5144-1's regeneration is exponentially quicker than 682's.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Interaction&nbsp;of&nbsp;SCP-5144-1&nbsp;and&nbsp;SCP-999</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Interaction&nbsp;of&nbsp;SCP-5144-1&nbsp;and&nbsp;SCP-999</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<div class="blockquote">
<p>SCP-5144-1 requested to meet with SCP-999. Video footage was taken of the interaction as normal.</p>
<p><strong>&lt;Begin Recording&gt;</strong></p>
<p>*SCP-5144-1 enters SCP-999's containment. No staff are present in the room. SCP-999 notices 5144-1 and squirms over to it.*</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Hello little guy.&quot; *5144-1 bent down to meet 999*</p>
<p><strong>999:</strong> &quot;Little squeaking noises&quot;</p>
<p><strong>Researcher watching interaction:</strong> &quot;Odd. It has never had a reaction like this to anyone.&quot;</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Huh, I do feel better. But why do I feel like I know this guy from somewhere?&quot;</p>
<p><strong>Researcher:</strong> &quot;What do you mean?&quot;</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;I know for a fact I haven't met him before but he somehow seems familiar. I can't explain it. Like, something about him feels very familiar but I don't know why. It's like that feeling I had with 3k.&quot;</p>
<p><strong>Researcher:</strong> &quot;3k?&quot;</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;3000. The big serpent lady who makes the amnestics.&quot;</p>
<p>*999 starts playing with 5144-1's tail flower, then falls back and sneezes because of the psychedelic pollen. The pollen has no effect on 999.*</p>
<p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Heh, what a funny creature you are.&quot;</p>
<p>*SCP-5144-1 continued to interact with 999, forming pieces of candy from the air and giving it to 999, for 10 minutes before leaving.*</p>
<p><strong>&lt;End Recording&gt;</strong></p>
</div>
