<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Other&nbsp;Cross&nbsp;Tests</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Other&nbsp;Cross&nbsp;Tests</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Addendum| Cross test SCP-173:</strong> Cross testing of SCP-5144-1 with SCP-173 to attempt to kill 5144-1 was attempted. SCP-5144-1 willingly entered the containment cell of 173 and let its neck get snapped. The test failed as 5144-1 remained alive. It was instructed to terminate the 173 clone on the spot and succeeded in vaporizing 80% of 173. This is the reason for the tremors felt throughout the site on the same day.</p>
<p><strong>Addendum| Cross test SCP-4162:</strong> SCP-5144-1 was deployed in close proximity to SCP-4162 after 4162 killed a D-class. SCP-4162 designated 5144-1 as its target and began approaching it. When SCP-5144-1 was in range of 4162, its skull suddenly exploded. 10 seconds later, SCP-5144-1's skull reformed. SCP-4162 did not designate it as its target again and moved toward a D-class.</p>
<p><strong>Addendum| Cross test SCP-2200-1:</strong> SCP-5144-1 was placed in SCP-2200-2's containment cell. SCP-2200-2 was instructed to attempt to terminate SCP-5144-1. After a few seconds of 2200-2 bickering, it agreed. SCP-5144-1 had its head removed by SCP-2200-1. 5144-1's head dematerialized and reformed back on its body. SCP-2200-2 was angered and attempted termination of 5144-1 three more times, all failed.</p>
<p><strong>Addendum| Cross test SCP-3660:</strong> SCP-5144-1 was exposed to SCP-3660 on its forearm. Upon contact with epidermis, SCP-5144-1 claimed to feel a small itch. SCP-3660 soon opened the skin of SCP-5144-1 and then detached. An opening about 5 meters in size had formed on the forearm. SCP-5144-1 reported feeling a stinging pain before it started bleeding from the opening. No entities exited 5144-1's body during this time. SCP-5144-1 continued to bleed for 2 minutes before the opening suddenly closed.</p>
<p><strong>Addendum| Cross test SCP-409:</strong> SCP-5144-1 was exposed to SCP-409. Upon contact with 409, 5144-1 reported a slight burning pain in its body. SCP-409 crystals began forming on its arm. 5 minutes into the test, SCP-5144-1's body is covered by crystals and suddenly shatters. The crystals then begin turning to dust, and SCP-5144-1 reformed from the dust particles.</p>
</div>
