<p><strong>Item #:</strong> SCP-5144-3</p>
<p><strong>AKA:</strong> The Star Jumper</p>
<p><strong>Object Class:</strong> Safe</p>
<p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> SCP-5144-3 is contained at Site-38 in SCP-5144's cell. It is an inanimate object and is easily contained. However its size was the determining factor in 5144's containment cell size.</p>
<p><strong>Description:</strong> 5144-3 is a large spaceship around ██ by ██ by ██ meters in size. This is why the containment cell is 100 by 50 by 40 meters in size. Whatever the ship is constructed of is too durable for any non-anomalous foundation weaponry to damage. However, 5144-3 has visible scorch marks and damage to its right thrusters and hull (See SCP-5144-1 interview for details).</p>
<p><strong>Bottom level:</strong> Located near the rear of the ship is the cargo bay door. Inside the cargo bay are metal crates of unknown &quot;fruits&quot; described 5144-1. The airlock opens directly into the bridge of the ship. In the center of the bridge is a 15 meter tall pedestal. Atop the pedestal is an open platform ,that 5144-1 has shown, activates a spherical hologram when 5144-1 is present. The hologram has the ability to detect 5144-1's thoughts and movements, moving exactly how he wishes it to. The hologram sphere glows a light blue and vaguely resembles an advanced computer setup. Ship diagnostics and status checks are visible on the hologram.</p>
<p><strong>Top level:</strong>On the sides of the bridge are metal grate steps leading to the top of the ship. Up in the top level, there is a balcony overviewing the bridge and is about 3 feet higher then the command platform. A large nuclear reactor is visibly exposed in the center of the top area, also glowing a light blue but substantially brighter in comparison to the control hologram. On the walls around the reactor are many lockers each containing different items. (See list of items below) In the rear top level of the ship was a single metal door opening into a hallway that connected to a bedroom, a spare bedroom, a bathroom, and a charging station for 5144-2.</p>
<p><strong>Anomalous Properties:</strong> SCP-5144-3 is a vehicle from another universe. The technology used in its construction is greatly evolved.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">List&nbsp;of&nbsp;sub-anomalous&nbsp;items&nbsp;in&nbsp;SCP-5144-3</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">List&nbsp;of&nbsp;sub-anomalous&nbsp;items&nbsp;in&nbsp;SCP-5144-3</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">The items below are identified as SCP-5144-3[A-Z]</span></strong></p>
<p><strong>5144-3A:</strong> Twenty cans of an unknown meat substance.</p>
<p><strong>5144-3B:</strong> An unopened wine bottle from [REDACTED] Winery, which does not exist.</p>
<p><strong>5144-3C:</strong> 3 World War 2 grade grenades. (Confiscated)</p>
<p><strong>5144-3D:</strong> A videotape of a foundation worker trapped on the moon after SCP-2399 destroyed earth.</p>
<p><strong>5144-3E:</strong> An Aztec ritual dagger with blood of Roman Emperor Caesar on it. (Confiscated)</p>
<p><strong>5144-3F:</strong> A photo album of SCP-5144-1 and a pink, humanoid entity.</p>
<p><strong>5144-3G:</strong> 7 liters of nutrient rich water.</p>
<p><strong>5144-3H:</strong> A sack of 37 coins with unknown etchings on them. SCP-5144-1 describes them as an alien currency.</p>
<p><strong>5144-3I:</strong> A small mirror that reflects an x-ray image of a user.</p>
<p><strong>5144-3J:</strong> A handgun, mechanical in nature, not resembling any model known. Handgun fires .50 caliber bullets without recoil. (SCP-5144-1 denied confiscation of item)</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
